      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "7a852ffb0f6ff0406b9fa6e3cc2db49ebcc5b986cc28be3af429425e682199f8",
        "2": "7a852ffb0f6ff0406b9fa6e3cc2db49ebcc5b986cc28be3af429425e682199f8",
        "3": "7a852ffb0f6ff0406b9fa6e3cc2db49ebcc5b986cc28be3af429425e682199f8",
        "4": "66838ce0d2e98d898368c7e0647aff49d26877d4176b284f7aa8d370798584f2",
        "5": "66838ce0d2e98d898368c7e0647aff49d26877d4176b284f7aa8d370798584f2",
        "6": "66838ce0d2e98d898368c7e0647aff49d26877d4176b284f7aa8d370798584f2",
        "7": "f568108edd2878f7cc74763c98089909d5b38a24046f2c96d3bd38c6c012a1e9",
        "8": "f568108edd2878f7cc74763c98089909d5b38a24046f2c96d3bd38c6c012a1e9",
        "9": "f568108edd2878f7cc74763c98089909d5b38a24046f2c96d3bd38c6c012a1e9"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09-s29-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The app uploads the bytes to S three. The event runs the indexer, which writes the searchable metadata separately. The object can be ready before the index row is.",
          "text_sha256": "d4a602e7889e44809e15f556eca595048b7cd8b64fa9c962bc7f2ea8228b803b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f8031ffe1b8e0bf10c8c9cbc02b47f735f3cb7dd2b1fe47bdd1cc5ad25581d88",
          "asset_sha256": "7a852ffb0f6ff0406b9fa6e3cc2db49ebcc5b986cc28be3af429425e682199f8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s29-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Find the tenant's reports for the date by querying the index, then use the returned key to get the chosen file from S three.",
          "text_sha256": "954e484a2053a9734ce862c9baeced158e2f9de117cd076e293b1a73fa8ac413",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "70e46c0fb53efda5f36437784719a8bd6d62866faaf4859a6da9954bd3e76251",
          "asset_sha256": "7a852ffb0f6ff0406b9fa6e3cc2db49ebcc5b986cc28be3af429425e682199f8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s29-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Handle duplicate or out-of-order events and reconcile missing rows. Enforce tenant access on both paths.",
          "text_sha256": "9c89a3669c25c04a2ce9538c896cbd5da1bad234489e2512151a13042e9fad0e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9c89a3669c25c04a2ce9538c896cbd5da1bad234489e2512151a13042e9fad0e",
          "asset_sha256": "7a852ffb0f6ff0406b9fa6e3cc2db49ebcc5b986cc28be3af429425e682199f8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s30-01",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "The browser asks CloudFront for an image. On a miss, CloudFront fetches it from the private S three origin. S three stores, not runs, the image.",
          "text_sha256": "9bcd4459562eac04551a60af8d8cdfb1c6612207e021188c487cb2b335a3fe3b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4f077bb654d1d06fc29c169b4da38345ba6ab8ddc78e0c8547995a9bc876f575",
          "asset_sha256": "66838ce0d2e98d898368c7e0647aff49d26877d4176b284f7aa8d370798584f2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s30-02",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "An order update goes to the application code, which validates it and writes the transaction to a database.",
          "text_sha256": "c3f323ee2378b7928cf50fc7ad4d54471efa86b2ffdc66faa25bba2d29b3259d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c3f323ee2378b7928cf50fc7ad4d54471efa86b2ffdc66faa25bba2d29b3259d",
          "asset_sha256": "66838ce0d2e98d898368c7e0647aff49d26877d4176b284f7aa8d370798584f2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s30-03",
          "slide": 6,
          "text": "The app first authorizes the photo upload, then signs a scoped request so the bytes go direct to S three.",
          "text_sha256": "789b3dfaf3d7daa09c83d07c328dfc2ed72c2cb9258da8b46970668bf419d727",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1307dab44ac32349660a60739e3a17a78b5a8b5707609f57c0d5ff47c509ff19",
          "asset_sha256": "66838ce0d2e98d898368c7e0647aff49d26877d4176b284f7aa8d370798584f2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s31-01",
          "slide": 7,
          "text": "If version three overwrote a good file, see whether version two still exists and the recovery role can read it.",
          "text_sha256": "7b3f04ddce28cd73b399d1a71d8166fb4fb9d6dacc410feb22c5844c566dfb4e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7b3f04ddce28cd73b399d1a71d8166fb4fb9d6dacc410feb22c5844c566dfb4e",
          "asset_sha256": "f568108edd2878f7cc74763c98089909d5b38a24046f2c96d3bd38c6c012a1e9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s31-02",
          "slide": 8,
          "text": "To resist destructive deletion, apply suitable Object Lock to required versions and consider an independent recovery boundary. A delete marker can still hide the current view.",
          "text_sha256": "669002a41405f4cfee6a43d190de7132f1e1f4d955134f2f2633bf2afa2160fe",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "669002a41405f4cfee6a43d190de7132f1e1f4d955134f2f2633bf2afa2160fe",
          "asset_sha256": "f568108edd2878f7cc74763c98089909d5b38a24046f2c96d3bd38c6c012a1e9"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s31-03",
          "slide": 9,
          "text": "For a Region outage, check replica lag, keys and permissions, then test an actual app read before relying on the replica.",
          "text_sha256": "4a1769327f607524206dc376304ab5c5bf4182f08b144f7df9173ea6c4d7e9ec",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4a1769327f607524206dc376304ab5c5bf4182f08b144f7df9173ea6c4d7e9ec",
          "asset_sha256": "f568108edd2878f7cc74763c98089909d5b38a24046f2c96d3bd38c6c012a1e9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "11",
      "revision": "m09p11-sap-m09-p10-p12-approved-review",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777",
        "2": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777",
        "3": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777",
        "4": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe",
        "5": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe",
        "6": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09-s32-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Start with how the app uses the data. Whole objects addressed by keys fit S three; shared files, block access and transactions need different semantics.",
          "text_sha256": "3876c4fd518450076ae732bfcd2ab983097abb9b4f36c17ca81b5e2bb4da659d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0d4d03f43232acfc87ee6cdf5bbda7725b203a5f0f65bcb014fb84e54ad432d2",
          "asset_sha256": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s32-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Choose storage and retention against the recovery deadline, not just the cheapest price.",
          "text_sha256": "f167835959052cc697e7b382be3fe53400b73a5fb2825696a12ba5731ea0ba76",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f167835959052cc697e7b382be3fe53400b73a5fb2825696a12ba5731ea0ba76",
          "asset_sha256": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s32-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Before calling it ready, confirm the app can reach, authorize and decrypt the read, and test the dependent event or index path.",
          "text_sha256": "dc5b0d5a232c6254d5df5dc28ebde52725bf74135e6dd0f4804041a12ef0f0e3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dc5b0d5a232c6254d5df5dc28ebde52725bf74135e6dd0f4804041a12ef0f0e3",
          "asset_sha256": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s33-01",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Local or block storage can suit a fleet that already runs web code; instance store is ephemeral and E B S is scoped to its Availability Zone.",
          "text_sha256": "77a49f6c22e3417ce7e732a84cdfe765321b62fe37040a43b2bdb2c5184a969c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b1f2327250fbc6f18d3e8469c10c43fcefc508a4c562a08edc30f8458c520035",
          "asset_sha256": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s33-02",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "If the fleet needs one shared file namespace, use EFS where it fits. You still run the web tier.",
          "text_sha256": "9f9d85ddbf058f4d6fd7f12ef8f12d5e77a3e50f65b6566ee220ecfcc4273653",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9f9d85ddbf058f4d6fd7f12ef8f12d5e77a3e50f65b6566ee220ecfcc4273653",
          "asset_sha256": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s33-03",
          "slide": 6,
          "text": "For static files alone, a CloudFront distribution can serve from a private S three object origin instead. Use Origin Access Control with the regular S three origin, not an S three website endpoint.",
          "text_sha256": "100f08c73a8049916ddd22c2ddb57ca8b341507c64998f7b1d5bc0bad962237c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "576574b82ff96f7175cf2e305311722e81b397ebe450d99447a4075669858972",
          "asset_sha256": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "12",
      "revision": "m09p12-sap-m09-p10-p12-approved-review",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b",
        "2": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b",
        "3": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18",
        "4": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18",
        "5": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f",
        "6": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f",
        "7": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c",
        "8": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c",
        "9": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09-s34-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The client uses one endpoint; S three routes the request by proximity among eligible regional buckets. It doesn't check where the object exists. If the selected bucket lacks the file, the read can fail.",
          "text_sha256": "f5326197e7cb3bd9882274af4afa7d5d375d9624751c7f1bce36886d0e31060b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a746520f798b9072b6623f8b38f09c1dffeff29d38abfa4e8ae352a49863a187",
          "asset_sha256": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s34-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Prepare data and key permissions in the destination before failover. Changing a route doesn't move or unlock the data.",
          "text_sha256": "77e964e30fcdce18f42435c87010028352b6cd80d291082a1daae23b5b3b9319",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6035ff94017777eae5fd8d7130a2f174de78cd3bdffaac11be404dd74275d47e",
          "asset_sha256": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s35-01",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Object Lambda could transform a response rather than rewrite the stored object. Since November 2025 it's limited to existing users and select ay double-you ess partners; a new design should evaluate the application, A P I or an eligible CloudFront path.",
          "text_sha256": "ef9e22419cc2c8784b71258fe80fce8ba39e545dd0431f6a37669a38b1ef2580",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6efbf1daca911583300192a50c14555273f56badbbf32fd4a667e67f850cb336",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s35-02",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Vault Lock applies to a legacy vault policy. S three Object Lock applies to object versions. Glacier storage classes affect storage and retrieval, not retention lock.",
          "text_sha256": "6525594c7402b324fedf30b14e713807dfd836f12ee76b12d86648c59b67ca20",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "47feb5d4c332ee043dc1d12fbbb3cdeaf696dbb5da876b557a8ca1fd849a4bf2",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s36-01",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "The app signs an operation for a specific bucket and key, then the client sends the signed request straight to S three without receiving ay double-you ess credentials.",
          "text_sha256": "11d32df04a5cd5c2f4acceb7b82f87a933475a4e0b5251168f0ebcbc2cc73bcf",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5fc8464b7b6d6ba5e4876dd28496ccd25da3c590108b7a10d648a8ab4818eccf",
          "asset_sha256": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s36-02",
          "slide": 6,
          "text": "One operation does not mean one use. Anyone holding the URL can repeat the permitted request until it expires or the signing credentials stop working. For uploads that must not overwrite an existing object, choose a unique key or require conditional creation.",
          "text_sha256": "bf1acd073fd1bc025a7d54976e1882979c7d8e9d806db55c684b599384c1c5b5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bf1acd073fd1bc025a7d54976e1882979c7d8e9d806db55c684b599384c1c5b5",
          "asset_sha256": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s37-01",
          "slide": 7,
          "text": "To see who called an object A P I, enable the relevant CloudTrail S three data events.",
          "text_sha256": "5850c34bc200c100adc28b73fde80e2b304901b3eeef596464254431b47ee5f1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "327ef396ca9d0a277afb0ae639231b836e8ad73cbd2634ff454acc7f40b5a2f3",
          "asset_sha256": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s37-02",
          "slide": 8,
          "text": "Server access logs record request details but arrive on a best-effort basis; a missing line alone proves nothing.",
          "text_sha256": "a4cf8cfb48859f8d407d67e1f46a42c984562c9c6fe54c1a37be1b781b833315",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a4cf8cfb48859f8d407d67e1f46a42c984562c9c6fe54c1a37be1b781b833315",
          "asset_sha256": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s37-03",
          "slide": 9,
          "text": "For trends, use request metrics or Storage Lens. A spike tells you where to investigate, not who made a specific call.",
          "text_sha256": "28dd190365da75786d4e2f9105ddd159af8b2cdd9430550cd9bd242227a89d04",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "28dd190365da75786d4e2f9105ddd159af8b2cdd9430550cd9bd242227a89d04",
          "asset_sha256": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
